  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A photograph from the High Line of a Chelsea street with a colourful mural of Mother Teresa and Gandhi, where a rooftop has a cartoon mountain drawn on it, buses and cars are redrawn as cartoons, and scribbled text covers a wall, signed 23.",
    "description": "A portrait format digital piece on a photograph inside a white border, signed Matt Crump 23 at lower right. Looking down from the High Line onto an avenue: glass towers at upper left, brick apartment blocks, and at right a building whose side wall carries a real colourful mural of two faces with a rainbow geometric pattern. Above it, a cream wall carries scribbled grey text like a fake inscription, and on the rooftop a cartoon has been drawn of a brown and blue mountain with a cloud and a chimney, with a drawn smoke plume rising into the real sky. In the street, cars and a bus are redrawn as white, grey and blue cartoon shapes, with a large blue and white cartoon bus and a yellow cab at the lower right beside a green construction fence. A small cartoon figure stands on the sidewalk at centre, and faceless pedestrians walk near the bus. Autumn trees line the avenue.",
    "impression": "The city already had a mural, so the drawing answers it with a mountain on the roof and fake scripture on the wall. The smoke plume rising into the real clouds is the nicest trick, a cartoon chimney feeding the actual sky. The soft bus in the corner keeps it friendly. A picture about a city covered in pictures.",
